# ==============================================================================
# Trivy Security Scanner Ignore List (.trivyignore)
# Databricks Hub-and-Spoke AWS Networking Architecture
# ==============================================================================
# This file defines approved exceptions for Trivy security checks in this
# repository, documenting the code ID, description, affected resources,
# and architectural justification for each exemption.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule ID:     AVD-AWS-0104
# Description: Security group rule allows unrestricted egress (0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0)
# Severity:    CRITICAL
# Target:      modules/01.networking/002.spoke_vpc/vpc_spoke_security_groups.tf
#              Resource: aws_security_group.default_spoke_sg
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Justification:
# 1. Functional Requirement: Databricks compute clusters in the Spoke VPC
#    require outbound connectivity on specific TCP ports (443 HTTPS for API/control
#    plane, 3306 for Hive Metastore, and 6666 for Secure Cluster Connectivity).
# 2. AWS Security Group Limitation: Security groups operate at Layer 4 and
#    only support IP/CIDR-based rules (not FQDN/domain names). External cloud
#    services and Databricks control plane endpoints use dynamic IP addresses,
#    necessitating destination 0.0.0.0/0 on those designated egress ports.
# 3. Compensating Control: Direct internet access is disabled for compute
#    subnets. All outbound traffic is routed through AWS Transit Gateway (TGW)
#    into the centralized Hub VPC. Inside the Hub VPC, AWS Network Firewall
#    enforces stateful Layer 7 Deep Packet Inspection (DPI) and strict domain
#    allowlists (SNI/FQDN filtering) before any traffic is allowed out to the NAT
#    Gateway, effectively mitigating data exfiltration risks.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AVD-AWS-0104

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule ID:     AVD-AWS-0164
# Description: Subnet assigns public IP addresses by default
#              (map_public_ip_on_launch = true)
# Severity:    HIGH
# Target:      modules/01.networking/003.hub_vpc/main.tf
#              Resource: aws_subnet.hub_nat_public_subnet
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Justification:
# 1. Architectural Role: The 'hub-nat-public' subnets are the designated public
#    perimeter subnets within the centralized Hub VPC. They directly interface
#    with the Internet Gateway (IGW) and host public egress NAT Gateways as well
#    as any potential bastion/management entry points.
# 2. Public IP Requirement: Resources deployed into public perimeter subnets
#    require public IP assignment by design to support internet routing and NAT
#    gateway operations.
# 3. Isolation of Compute: All Databricks compute instances and Transit Gateway
#    attachments reside exclusively in private subnets (map_public_ip_on_launch = false)
#    with no direct public IP assignment or direct inbound connectivity from the
#    internet.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AVD-AWS-0164
